    "narrative": "The objective for Ghost Ride the WHIP today is to capitalize on favorable matchups against poor pitching, headlined by **Corbin Carroll** (87.14) and **Vinnie Pasquantino** (75.07). **Corbin Carroll** is our primary engine against Lowder; with a projected 5.25 xERA and a dynamic platoon advantage, he is in prime position to pad our SB totals and run production. Similarly, **Vinnie Pasquantino** draws a soft landing against Burrows, where his 14% platoon boost and strong order placement make him an elite UTIL play. **James Wood** (67.30) and **Gabriel Moreno** (71.10) also anchor the daily floor, as both benefit from soft pitching matchups and top-tier order placement that maximizes their opportunity for counting stats.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision today involved the final utility spot, where **Alex Freeland** (45.91) narrowly missed the cut behind **Henry Bolte** (57.08). While **Alex Freeland** offers switch-hitting versatility, his deep-order placement suppressed his efficiency score compared to **Henry Bolte**, whose platoon edge against the southpaw Freeland provides more upside in a high-variance spot. We are also monitoring the risk associated with **Brice Turang** (53.24) and **Jose Caballero** (44.40); both face pitchers with elite defensive metrics\u2014Nola and Gausman, respectively\u2014which significantly hampers their base-stealing ceiling despite their sprint speeds. We are betting that **Brice Turang** and **Jose Caballero** can manufacture runs through situational discipline, but they remain lower-tier plays today given the strength of the opposing batteries.",
